From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:52:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: HDR over the tunnel leaves the vendor slot
 of the stream free, as i915 does

linux-9975 says that HDR over the tunnel sends no vendor packet and leaves
the slot free, and i915 turns its vendor DIP off for it; but
amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_fill_stream() only left the Dolby VSIF out, and kept in
vsp_infopacket what create_stream_for_sink() had made for the mode: the
HDMI vendor InfoFrame with the HDMI VIC of 3840x2160 and 4096x2160 at 24,
25 and 30 Hz (next to the CTA VIC that the tunnel puts in the AVI
InfoFrame), or the 2D one that follows a 3D mode.

The tunnel now empties the slot: the AVI InfoFrame has the CTA VIC, and
HDR10+ has a packet of its own. The Dolby Vision tunnels put their VSIF
there as before, and a stream without the tunnel does not go through this
function: plain HDMI and 3D keep their vendor InfoFrame as before. Kodi
sends HDR over the tunnel at 2160p50 and 60 only, where the mode has no
HDMI VIC.

Host test: the vendor block of amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_fill_stream() and
amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_infopacket() taken from the source and run with
stand-ins for the packers, over HDR over the tunnel and the three Dolby
Vision tunnels, and the one call of the function, for a connector that
asks for the tunnel. Without this change the two cases of HDR over the
tunnel whose stream had a vendor InfoFrame fail, and so does a mutant
without the clearing. W=1 on amdgpu: no warning. Not run on hardware.
---
 .../gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c   | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
index 6b19feecd..c36faa6f8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -1792,6 +1792,14 @@ int amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_fill_stream(struct drm_connector *connector,
 		ret = amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_infopacket(buf, len, &stream->vsp_infopacket);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
+	} else {
+		/*
+		 * Hades: ... nor the vendor InfoFrame that create_stream_for_sink() made for the
+		 * mode (the HDMI VIC of 4K at 24, 25 and 30 Hz, or the 2D one after a 3D mode): the
+		 * AVI InfoFrame has the CTA VIC, and the slot is free, as i915 leaves it
+		 * (intel_hdmi_compute_hdmi_infoframe())
+		 */
+		memset(&stream->vsp_infopacket, 0, sizeof(stream->vsp_infopacket));
 	}
 
 	stream->timing.vic = vic;
